3. Architectural Design
EduGenie can follow a three-layer architecture.
Presentation Layer
Responsible for interaction with students.
Main components:
• Login/Register
• Dashboard
• AI Chat interface
• File upload interface
• Quiz interface
• Flashcard interface
• Progress dashboard
• Study planner
Application Layer
Acts as the main processing layer.
Responsibilities:
• Authenticate users.
• Validate requests.
• Communicate with Gemini.
• Process uploaded materials.
• Generate quizzes.
• Evaluate answers.
• Store learning results.
• Generate recommendations.
Data Layer
Responsible for persistent information.
Stores:
• User profiles
• Chat history
• Uploaded-material metadata
• Quiz questions
• Quiz attempts
• Scores
• Flashcards
• Learning progress
• Study plans
 
