16. Security Design
Security should be considered at every layer.
Authentication
• Firebase Authentication can manage user accounts.
• Passwords should not be stored directly by the application.
Authorization
Users should only be able to access their own:
• Study materials
• Chat history
• Quiz results
• Progress information
API Security
The Gemini API key should not be exposed in frontend code.
Instead:
Frontend
  ↓
Backend
  ↓
Gemini API
File Security
Uploaded files should be:
• Validated.
• Stored securely.
• Associated with the authenticated user.
• Protected from unauthorized access.
 
17. Error Handling Design
EduGenie should handle common failures gracefully.
Problem
System Response
Invalid login
Display authentication error
Unsupported file
Ask user to upload a supported file
Large file
Display file-size warning
Gemini unavailable
Display temporary service message
Empty question
Ask user to enter a question
Database failure
Display retry option
Network failure
Display connection message
 
